nd a well-crafted packet that could trigger memory exhaustion in the server process by specifying multiple references. We now reject these as malformed and curb the memory amplification vector as a result.","Severity":"HIGH","CweIDs":["CWE-405"],"VendorSeverity":{"redhat":3},"CVSS":{"redhat":{"V3Vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","V3Score":7.5}},"References":["https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-97031","https://go.dev/cl/847312","https://go.dev/issue/81855","https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/U2fTuyDJznI","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-97031","https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-6607","https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-97031"],"PublishedDate":"2026-10-08T23:17:06.037Z","LastModifiedDate":"2026-10-09T16:35:35.9Z"}]}]}
